From 3a38a4c24dd2eaa04b19bcf95b677cdfaff854bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 17:53:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.9.2: Devices page - MLO link awareness + offline
 connection-dash fix

Two metal-reported Rung A (Device Identity Manager) fixes:

1. Offline/never-seen devices printed a literal "&mdash;" in the Connection
   column: that cell was the one dash passed through esc(), so & became &amp;.
   Build the connection cell as HTML like the other dash cells. (Worst for
   upgraders: a reserved device that has not associated since the flash has no
   band yet, so the placeholder showed until first connect.)

2. Wi-Fi 7 MLO: wl assoclist reports each affiliated per-link MAC (locally-
   administered, lease-less) so an MLO client surfaced as several scary
   "Private addr / No lease" orphan rows. do_reaper_dev_cgi now detects MLO
   fronthaul active (mld_enable=1 + non-empty mld{0,1,2}_ifnames) and flags such
   stations mlo_link; the page labels them "MLO . <band>" with an explanatory
   tooltip (RDEV_87) and stops counting them under Unnamed / Randomized /
   Needs-attention. Zero behavior change when MLO is off. Row-merging into one
   device per MLD is a follow-up (needs the driver link->MLD map).
